{"description":"Expose the EKA feedback loop as MCP tools per req:eka-mcp-production revision 4 §8.2 decision 4: feedback_new, feedback_list, and feedback_publish mirroring the CLI subcommands (eka feedback new/list/publish, ADR-026 feedback module). Rationale: agents operating EKA day-to-day are the first to discover tool limitations; filing feedback must not require leaving the MCP transport.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. Tools mirror CLI subcommand semantics exactly: feedback_new creates a local draft under EKA_HOME/feedback (YAML frontmatter + markdown body), feedback_list lists drafts and published reports deterministically, feedback_publish files a draft as a GitHub issue on the fixed target repository.\n2. ADR-026 invariants preserved verbatim: feedback NEVER enters the canonical store and never becomes engineering knowledge; no CKO is produced by any of the three tools.\n3. Publish constraints inherited unchanged: release-binary requirement enforced with deterministic refusal otherwise; missing/invalid token refuses deterministically naming the remediation (never a raw HTTP error); token material never appears in tool outputs, errors, or logs.\n4. Error messages follow the established refusal-class policy (no internal paths, no store details).\n5. Conformance suite extended for the three tools (list-call semantics + refusal cases: unauthenticated publish, invalid draft id); fuzz cases for malformed args.\n6. Docs updated (tool table, mcp-boundary.md) including an explicit statement that feedback is meta-information outside the knowledge model.\n7. Full gates green in eka-mcp: go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test ./...","debtRationale":""}